# Git commit message format

**Content** — what the message should *say* (e.g. commit messages explain the
*why*, not just the *what*, intent of the body): follow
**`rules/ao-git-workflow-and-versioning-rule.mdc`**, especially **Descriptive
Messages**.

This file defines **mechanical format** only. For **subject-line shape** and
**72-column layout**, it **supersedes** Conventional Commits examples (`feat:`,
`fix:`) elsewhere when they conflict.

When the user **does** ask for a commit, use this **subject line** shape (one
line, **72 characters or fewer** when practical):

```text
<TICKET> <TYPE>: <short imperative description>
```

## Parts

- **`<TICKET>`** — Issue id from context (e.g. `ATC-2363`). Prefer the branch
  name (`ATC-2363-FEATURE-…`) or what the user/Jira ticket states. If unknown,
  ask once instead of inventing a number.
- **`<TYPE>`** — Short uppercase category, e.g. `FEATURE`, `FIX`, `REFACTOR`,
  `MODEL`, `DEV ENV`, `INTERNAL`, `DOCS`, `TEST`. Match types already used on
  the branch when obvious.
- **`<description>`** — Imperative, specific; trailing period only if the team
  already uses full sentences there.

### Subject line examples

```text
ATC-2363 FEATURE: Activity History - Telemarketer Dropdown
ATC-2363 DEV ENV: Add telemarketer seeds
ATC-2363 REFACTOR: Extract quote activity history edit policy load
ATC-2363 MODEL: Add telemarketer associations on computed and fact models
```

**Do not** switch to unrelated formats (e.g. Conventional Commits `feat:` only)
unless the user explicitly requests that repo’s alternate convention for this
task.

## Line width

- **72 characters** maximum per line for the subject and for every body line
  (including wrapped continuation lines of a bullet).
- Wrap long lines at word boundaries when a line would exceed 72 characters.

## Body layout (optional)

- Use a **blank line** after the subject when there is a body.
- **Bullets** start with `- ` when the body is a list; wrap to 72 columns.

Whether and how much body to add is **content** — see
**`rules/ao-git-workflow-and-versioning-rule.mdc`**.

When summarizing a commit in chat, mirror the same **shape** and **line
width**.

## Format examples

### Subject-only

```text
ATC-2423 FIX: Null-safe quote lookup when policy number missing
```

